# REAL (binary32) arithmetic, ed.3 table 30 / ed.2 table 24, and real
# literals (ed.3 6.3.2 table 5: a decimal point, an optional exponent, an
# optional `REAL#` prefix). Values compared within 1e-6 relative (SPEC.md),
# which absorbs binary32 rounding (0.1 + 0.2 is 0.3000000119 in binary32).
# Records keep y <> 0 (see undefined/real_div_zero).
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: x y
outputs: sum diff prod quot neg lit1 lit2 lit3
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.2.5.1 table 30 (arithmetic), 6.3.2 table 5 (real literals)
---
0 x=1.5 y=0.25        => sum=1.75 diff=1.25 prod=0.375 quot=6.0 neg=-1.5 lit1=1000.0 lit2=1.5 lit3=-0.025
1 x=1.0 y=3.0         => sum=4.0 diff=-2.0 prod=3.0 quot=0.3333333 neg=-1.0 lit1=1000.0 lit2=1.5 lit3=-0.025
2 x=0.1 y=0.2         => sum=0.3 diff=-0.1 prod=0.02 quot=0.5 neg=-0.1 lit1=1000.0 lit2=1.5 lit3=-0.025
3 x=1.0E10 y=1.0E10   => sum=2.0E10 diff=0.0 prod=1.0E20 quot=1.0 neg=-1.0E10 lit1=1000.0 lit2=1.5 lit3=-0.025
4 x=-2.5 y=4.0        => sum=1.5 diff=-6.5 prod=-10.0 quot=-0.625 neg=2.5 lit1=1000.0 lit2=1.5 lit3=-0.025
